nd  it's also clear that they have no idea  what this pager is we then see a scene  with Captain America black widow war  machine and Bruce Banner looking at the  pager Banner says that it was sending a  signal and then it finally stopped  Captain America is confused about why it  stopped because they now have it plugged  into where it doesn't need a battery war  machine confirms that it is plugged in  but it still just stopped  Captain America says reboot it so it  signals again but Bruce Banner steps in  and says we don't even know what this is  but Black Widow cuts in and says  fury did just do it please obviously  natasha has worked right alongside with  fury for many many years and is one of  the people that she trusts the most  so since Nick Fury is one of the people  that she trusts the most she trusts that  whatever device this is it's for good  she then tells him tell me when you get  a signal I want to know who's on the  other side of that thing she turns  around to leave and right when she turns  around she sees Captain Marvel standing  right in front of her in which Captain  Marvel says where's fury and then of  course it says Captain Marvel will  return in Avengers in game so there are  a few things to note about this  post-credit scene one is that this  happens really early on in avengers  endgame we know this because Captain  America still has his beard and they're  tallying the deaths of all the people  who fell victim to the snap still  another thing that is very clear is that  the pager is blinking until Captain  Marvel shows up and when the pager stops  in the post-credits scene that is  because she has arrived at the Avengers  facility so it is no longer signaling  her and then of course she pops up  immediately after it also appears that  the Avengers have no idea who she is so  Nick Fury has never told them about  Captain Marvel at any point in time  another thing is that since this takes  place probably very early on in Avengers  in game that 